Hévéa Reduced Sphere
====================

This repository implements a reduced-sphere convex-integration experiment and
its Wolfram Language interface.

The generic corrugation, numerical integration, mesh-output ideas and parts of
the implementation were adapted from the Hévéa project:

  https://github.com/HeveaProject/Hevea

The upstream README credits the original Hévéa code to Vincent Borrelli,
Saïd Jabrane, Francis Lazarus and Boris Thibert. Hévéa is distributed under
the GNU General Public License version 3. This derivative repository is
distributed under the same license; see LICENSE.

The sphere-specific mathematical construction follows:

  Bartzos, Borrelli, Denis, Lazarus, Rohmer and Thibert,
  "An Explicit Isometric Reduction of the Unit Sphere into an Arbitrarily
  Small Ball", Foundations of Computational Mathematics (2017),
  DOI: 10.1007/s10208-017-9360-1.

The reduced-sphere profile, characteristic-flow implementation, numerical
certificates, CMake integration and Wolfram Language wrapper in this repository
are a separate reimplementation. They are not an official release of the
paper's authors or of the Hévéa project.
